ag B., Plez B., Homeier D.)",106],["\"J/BaltA/11/441/table4\"","Interstellar extinction and distances for stars observed by Hipparcos ( Zdanavicius J., Zdanavicius K.)",100],["\"J/A+A/520/A89/table27\"","HIPPARCOS photometry, Perryman et al. (1997, I/239) ( Mayer P., Harmanec P., Wolf M., Bozic H., Slechta M.)",89],["\"J/ApJS/150/455/table2\"","Hipparcos doubles ( Gould A., Chaname J.)",84],["\"J/AJ/162/181/table6\"","Hipparcos IAD measurements ( Llop-sayson J., Wang J.J., Ruffio J.-B., et al.)",78],["\"J/AJ/134/1916/table1\"","Hipparcos intermediate astrometric data for HR 6046 ( Torres G.)",78],["\"J/A+A/329/943/table7\"","*F & G stars on or near the main sequence data (as in table3 but with Hipparcos parallax) ( Ng Y.K., Bertelli G.)",76],["\"J/AJ/128/463/table6\"","Early-type M dwarfs from the revised NLTT: Hipparcos stars ( Reid I.N., Cruz K.L., Allen P., Mungall F., Kilkenny D., Liebert J., Hawley S.L., Fraser O.J., Covey K.R., Lowrance P., Kirkpatrick J.D., Burgasser A.J.)",71],["\"J/A+A/464/641/table6\"","Relative position compared to the Hipparcos/CCDM data ( Lampens P., Strigachev A., Duval D.)",63],["\"J/ApJ/792/119/table5\"","The Data of Our Non-Hipparcos and Serendipitous Pairs ( Deacon N.R., Liu M.C., Magnier E.A., et al.)",62],["\"J/BaltA/10/481/table13a\"","Halo and thick disk Hipparcos binaries with orbital transition ( Bartkevicius A., Gudas A.)",54],["\"J/A+AS/133/197/table5\"","Hipparcos Photometry for Groups of B, A, and F stars. ( Adelman S.J., Pi C.-L.M., Rayle K.)",49],["\"J/A+AS/124/157/table2\"","48 stars with absolute proper motion for the calibration of the Hipparcos proper motion system (Equinox J2000, Epoch 1950) ( Geffert M., Klemola A.R., Hiesgen M., Schmoll J.)",48],["\"J/AJ/121/3224/table4\"","Unresolved Hipparcos double stars ( Mason B.D., Hartkopf W.I., Holdenried E.R., Rafferty T.J.)",47],["\"J/AJ/133/906/table23\"","Radio star positions, uncertainties and offsets from Hipparcos (tables 2 and 3 of the paper) ( Boboltz D.A., Fey A